!Sample_title = E12.5 male Tet1-KO PGC RNA-Seq Replicate 2
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM2041490
!Sample_status = Public on Mar 07 2018
!Sample_submission_date = Jan 19 2016
!Sample_last_update_date = May 15 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = E12.5 male Tet1-KO PGC
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genetic background: Tet1-het GOF18∆PE-EGFP x Tet1-het GOF18∆PE-EGFP
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: Tet1-KO
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: E12.5
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = gender: male
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: PGC
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For study of Tet1-KO PGCs, total RNA from sorted PGCs isolated from individual Tet1-KO or wild type embryos was isolated using ZR-Duet DNA-RNA MiniPrep kit (Zymo), and RNA from between two to six embryos (equivalent to 1,000 to 8,000 cells) of the same genotype, stage and sex was pooled and concentrated to 6 µL final volume using the RNA Clean and Concentrator 5 kit (Zymo). For study of wild type PGCs isolated from embryos produced by crossing MF1 females with GOF18ΔPE-EGFP males, total RNA from 600-1,000 sorted E10.5 PGCs was isolated using the Nucleospin RNA XS kit (Macherey-Nagel).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = cDNA synthesis and amplification (15 cycles) was performed with the SMARTer Ultra Low Input RNA kit (Clontech) using between 100 pg and 3ng total RNA and following the manufacturer’s instructions. The amplified cDNA was fragmented by a Covaris S2 sonicator (Covaris) and following the manufacturer’s instructions. Sheared cDNA was converted to sequencing libraries using the NEBNext DNA Library Prep kit (NEB), following the manufacturer’s instructions and using 15 cycles of amplification. The libraries were purified by AMPure XP beads (Beckman-Coulter) and sequenced on the Illumina HiSeq 2500 instrument.
!Sample_description = RNA-Seq of primordial germ cells
!Sample_description = processed data file: E10_E12_E14_GeneCounts.txt
!Sample_data_processing = For study of Tet1-KO and Tet1-WT PGCs Illumina and Smart-seq adapters from the sequencing reads were first trimmed using Trimmomatic. Trimmomatic produces three fastq output files, one with paired end reads (PE) and two (F and R) with reads whose mate did not pass trimming criteria; PE, F and R fastq files were aligned separately and BAM files were merged at the end. For RNA-Seq libraries derived from PGCs isolated from embryos produced by crossing MF1 females with GOF18ΔPE-EGFP males, fastq files generated from output of next generation sequencing were used directly for alignment. RNA-Seq reads were aligned to the mouse genome (mm9, NCBI build 37) with Bowtie (version 0.12.8) and Tophat (version 2.0.2 with options -N 2 --b2-very-sensitive --b2-L 25. Annotations from Ensembl Gene version 67 were used as gene model with Tophat. Read counts per annotated gene were computed using HTSeq (version 0.5.3p9).
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm9
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: .txt files report gene counts
!Sample_platform_id = GPL17021
!Sample_contact_name = Peter,,Hill
!Sample_contact_email = peter.hill1@imperial.ac.uk
!Sample_contact_institute = Imperial College London
!Sample_contact_address = Kensington
!Sample_contact_city = London
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = SW7 2AZ
!Sample_contact_country = United Kingdom
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 2500
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
